_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 39
---
order: 39
---
short_label: I.39
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Equal triangles which are on the same base and on the same side are also in the same parallels.
----
proof:

Let {ABC} and {DBC} be equal triangles which are on the same base {BC} and on the same side of it. Join {AD}. [!just I.Post.1]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="260" height="210" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="I.39 diagram" src="propI39.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // A reductio, so the hypothetical apparatus (E, AE, EC) is deferred to the
    // slide that supposes it, and dropped again at the close — the walk ends on
    // the clean true figure. Colour carries the argument: ABC and DBC are the
    // equal pair, so they share cyan; EBC, the intruder the supposition forces
    // in, is orange. E rides on BD, which puts triangle EBC strictly INSIDE
    // triangle DBC — that containment is Euclid's "the greater equals the
    // less", visible rather than merely asserted.
    //
    // Fills are gated pairwise so each comparison is read against one other
    // region, never two: slide 4 shows ABC vs EBC (@I.37), slide 5 shows DBC vs
    // EBC (the contradiction). The regions are fill-only and initiallyHidden —
    // the original figure draws outlines and no fills, and the triangle sides
    // are declared as black lines in their own right so the outlines stand
    // whichever fills are gated off.
    var CORE  = ["A","B","C","D","BC","AB","AC","BD","CD"];
    var BASE  = CORE.concat(["ABC","BCD"]);
    var JOIN  = BASE.concat(["AD"]);
    var FRAME = CORE.concat(["AD","E","AE","CE","EB"]);
    var HYP   = FRAME.concat(["ABC","BCD"]);
    var CMP1  = FRAME.concat(["ABC","EBC"]);
    var CMP2  = FRAME.concat(["BCD","EBC"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "I.39",
        elements: [
            "B;point;free;40,170",
            "C;point;free;220,170",
            "A;point;free;80,40",
            // Invisible carrier: the parallel to BC through A. D slides on it,
            // so the figure at rest satisfies the proposition's conclusion —
            // the reductio's E is what departs from it.
            "AD';line;parallel;A,B,C;0;0;0",
            "D;point;lineSlider;AD',210,40",
            // The supposition's point: E slides along BD, so EBC nests inside DBC.
            "E;point;lineSlider;B,D,165,40",
            // Base, the join AD, and the two triangles' remaining sides.
            "BC;line;connect;B,C",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            // The supposed parallel through A, and the join EC.
            "AE;line;connect;A,E",
            "CE;line;connect;C,E",
            // EB is a sub-segment of BD (E lies on it); hover target only.
            "EB;line;connect;E,B;0;0;0",
            // Regions. The equal pair shares cyan; the supposition's EBC is orange.
            "ABC;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;0;cyan",
            "BCD;polygon;triangle;B,C,D;0;0;0;cyan",
            "EBC;polygon;triangle;E,B,C;0;0;0;orange"
        ],
        aliases: { "DBC": "BCD", "EC": "CE", "BA": "AB", "CA": "AC", "DB": "BD",
                   "DC": "CD", "EA": "AE", "BE": "EB", "DA": "AD", "CB": "BC" },
        initiallyHidden: ["ABC","BCD","EBC"],
        deferDraggables: ["E"],
        slides: [
            { text: "Let {ABC} and {DBC} be equal triangles which are on the same base {BC} and on the same side of it.",
              visible: BASE,
              highlighted: ["ABC","DBC","BC"] },
            { text: "Join {AD}. I say that {AD} is parallel to {BC}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["AD","BC"],
              transition: { animations: [ { elem: "AD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "If not, draw {AE} through the point {A} parallel to the straight line {BC}, and join {EC}.",
              visible: HYP,
              highlighted: ["AE","EC"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AE", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "CE", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.31" }, { ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Then the triangle {ABC} equals the triangle {EBC}, for it is on the same base {BC} with it and in the same parallels.",
              visible: CMP1,
              highlighted: ["ABC","EBC","BC"],
              transition: { animations: [ { elem: "EBC", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.37" }] },
            { text: "But {ABC} equals {DBC}, therefore {DBC} also equals {EBC} — the greater equals the less, which is impossible.",
              visible: CMP2,
              highlighted: ["DBC","EBC"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "C.N.1" }] },
            { text: "Therefore {AE} is not parallel to {BC}.",
              visible: HYP,
              highlighted: ["AE","BC"] },
            { text: "Similarly we can prove that neither is any other straight line except {AD}. Therefore {AD} is parallel to {BC}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["AD","BC"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.31":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI31/",
        "I.37":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI37/",
        "C.N.1":    "/elements/books/bookI/commonnotions/cn1/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

I say that {AD} is parallel to {BC}.

If not, draw {AE} through the point {A} parallel to the straight line {BC}, and join {EC}. [!just I.31, I.Post.1]

Therefore the triangle {ABC} equals the triangle {EBC}, for it is on the same base {BC} with it and in the same parallels. [!just I.37]

But {ABC} equals {DBC}, therefore {DBC} also equals {EBC}, the greater equals the less, which is impossible. [!just C.N.1]

Therefore {AE} is not parallel to {BC}.

Similarly we can prove that neither is any other straight line except {AD}, therefore {AD} is parallel to {BC}.

Therefore *equal triangles which are on the same base and on the same side are also in the same parallels.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
<br clear="all">
----
guide:

This is a partial converse to proposition @I.37, only partial since the two triangles {ABC} and {DBC} have to be on the same side of the line {BC}. If they weren't, then of course {AD} would not be parallel to {BC} but instead cross it at the midpoint

#### Use of Proposition 39

This proposition is used in @VI.2.
